In article <211@scorn.sco.COM> davidbe@sco.COM (The Cat in the Hat) writes:
>Running 3.0 patchlevel 5...
>So here I am, this first level character, and the first thing I do is 
>quaff one of my potions.  A ghost appears (first named Kay, then named
>davidbe).  I regain my composure in time, so I run to the up stairs and
>climb (I don't like dying or quitting).  With the unfriendly ghost next
>to me I climb and find that "You and the ghost davidbe escaped the
>dungeon with 54 points."  
>So is the ghost gone?  Should it have run off with me?  And should it have
>had my name or Kay's?
>Just curious...

Ohmigod.  Another LONG-standing bug.

The ghost name is correct; this behavior was programmed in (why, I don't
know).

It should not have run off with you though.  The problem is that ghosts
follow you up and down levels, and that you get points for pets which leave
the dungeon with you.  But the code just checks everything which leaves the
dungeon with you, pet or not...
